+### `os-window-always-on-top-changed` — Stable
+
+Fires when a window starts or stops being [kept on top](#keep-on-top--stable) — from the title bar's pin or from `windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop()`. A call that leaves the flag where it was fires nothing.
+
+```javascript
+document.addEventListener( 'os-window-always-on-top-changed', ( e ) => {
+    const { windowId, alwaysOnTop } = e.detail;
+    if ( windowId === 'my-plugin-monitor' ) {
+        setCompactLayout( alwaysOnTop );
+    }
+} );
+```
+
+**`detail` shape:**
+
+```typescript
+{
+    windowId:    string,
+    alwaysOnTop: boolean,   // the new state
+}
+```
+
+Companion `wp.hooks` action: `HOOKS.WINDOW_ALWAYS_ON_TOP_CHANGED` (`os.window.always-on-top-changed`).
+
+---
+
@@ -918,0 +945 @@ manager.raise( windowId: string ): void;                                 // rest
+manager.setAlwaysOnTop( windowId: string, enabled: boolean ): void;      // keep above every window that isn't; unknown ids are a no-op
@@ -1000,0 +1028,21 @@ manager.moveWindowToDesktop( windowId: string, desktopId: string ): boolean;
+#### Keep on top — Stable
+
+A window **kept on top** paints above every window that is not, even while another window is focused or a new one opens. The user toggles it with the pin at the front of the title bar's control cluster (`core/keep-on-top`); code calls `setAlwaysOnTop()` and reads the window's `alwaysOnTop` property.
+
+```javascript
+const manager = wp.os.windowManager;
+manager.setAlwaysOnTop( 'my-plugin-monitor', true );
+manager.getById( 'my-plugin-monitor' ).alwaysOnTop; // true
+```
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| **Several at once** | Any number of windows can be kept on top. Among themselves they stack in focus order, exactly as ordinary windows do below them. |
+| **Focus** | Unchanged. Focusing an ordinary window makes it the focused window — `isFocused()`, `getFocused()`, alt-tab and `os-window-focused` all agree — it just paints under the windows kept on top. Turning the flag on does not focus the window. |
+| **Turning it off** | The window drops back to its place in the ordinary stack; nothing else moves. |
+| **Child windows** | A child of a window kept on top rides with its owner, so it is never buried under the window it blocks. |
+| **Fullscreen** | A fullscreen window still paints above everything, windows kept on top included. |
+| **Session** | Part of the window's session entry (`alwaysOnTop: true`, written only when on), so it survives a reload. |
+
+Changes fire [`os-window-always-on-top-changed`](#os-window-always-on-top-changed--stable) and the `os.window.always-on-top-changed` action. Hide the pin on one window with `appearance.controls.hide: [ 'core/keep-on-top' ]`, or everywhere with `unregisterWindowControl( 'core/keep-on-top' )`; `setAlwaysOnTop()` keeps working either way.
+
